  "id": "COMPOUND:30081 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One and SMMC-7721, mediated through multiple targets. The compound is directly linked to VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets SMMC-7721, indicating a possible pathway of action. Additionally, Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One is associated with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is also targeted by Ginsenoside R10 and Anolobine, all of which ultimately act on SMMC-7721. These findings suggest that Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition or modulation of SMMC-7721. The evidence is supported by a chain of targets, but the exact mechanism by which these targets influence SMMC-7721 remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
